</div>
  <p>To change the position in the same manner, use <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlMoveToTarget" target="_blank">llMoveToTarget</a>. For physical objects a range between .2 and 1 is good for both parameters.</p>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>In Non-Physical objects this function operates effectively the same as <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetLocalRot" target="_blank">llSetLocalRot</a>.</li>
    <li><b>damping</b> seems to be capped at 1.0; greater values are reduced to 1.0 <i>(Tested 21 October 2010 on server version 10.10.18.212360)</i></li>
    <li>The minimum value for <b>strength</b> seems to be 0.0445 for the function to have any effect.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
  <p>Point the prim&#39;s positive y axis (<i>&lt;0.0, 1.0, 0.0&gt;</i>) towards a position on the sim</p>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//-- where vPosTarget is the global position of the object you want to "look" at
llRotLookAt( llRotBetween( <0.0,1.0,0.0>, llVecNorm( vPosTarget - llGetPos() ) ), 1.0, 0.4 ); // Point +Y axis towards vPosTarget`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>vPosTarget - llGetPos()</b> converts the global coordinates of the objects, to a local distance and direction from the object pointing</li>
    <li>Per <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlRotBetween" target="_blank">llRotBetween</a> article:
    <ul>
      <li><b>llRotBetween</b> returns a scaled rotation, unless both inputs are equal magnitude (e.g. unit vector).</li>
      <li>The use of <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlVecNorm" target="_blank">llVecNorm</a> reduces the magnitude to 1 (so that both are equal magnitude), preventing errors.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Constraining the Rotation to One Axis</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local detected = ll.DetectedPos(0)
local pos = ll.GetPos()
ll.RotLookAt(ll.RotBetween(vector(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), ll.VecNorm(vector(detected.x, detected.y, pos.z) - pos)), 1.0, 0.4)`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector detected = llDetectedPos( 0 );
      vector pos = llGetPos();
      llRotLookAt( llRotBetween( <0.0, 1.0, 0.0>, llVecNorm( <detected.x, detected.y, pos.z> - pos ) ), 1.0, 0.4 );`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Useful Snippets</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If you want a (mostly) smooth <i>constant</i> (rather than damped) rate of motion in a non-physical object try this</li>
  </ul>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function integer(s) return tonumber(string.match(s, "^%s*([-+]?%d+)")) or 0 end

---- Rotates Object to vRotTarget at vFltRate (in radians per second
---- vFltRate < ~0.00000003rad/sec, (~0.00002deg/sec) will result in errors (and is just too slow anyway)
---- vFltRate >= (PI * 5.0)rad/sec, (900deg/sec) will result in a single snap move to vRotTarget
local function uSteppedRotLookAt(vRotTarget, vFltRate)
    if (integer((function() vFltRate = (ll.AngleBetween(ll.GetLocalRot(), vRotTarget) / (vFltRate / 5.0)) return vFltRate end)())) ~= 0 then
        local vRotStep = ll.AxisAngle2Rot(ll.Rot2Axis(vRotTarget / ll.GetLocalRot()), (1.0 / vFltRate) * ll.Rot2Angle(vRotTarget / ll.GetLocalRot()))
        vFltRate = integer(vFltRate)
        repeat
            ll.SetLocalRot(vRotStep * ll.GetLocalRot())
        until not (((function() vFltRate -= 1 return vFltRate end)() ~= 0))
    end
    ll.SetLocalRot(vRotTarget)
end  ---- for fixed time on any rotation try llSetKeyframedMotion
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//-- Rotates Object to vRotTarget at vFltRate (in radians per second
//-- vFltRate < ~0.00000003rad/sec, (~0.00002deg/sec) will result in errors (and is just too slow anyway)
//-- vFltRate >= (PI * 5.0)rad/sec, (900deg/sec) will result in a single snap move to vRotTarget
uSteppedRotLookAt( rotation vRotTarget, float vFltRate ){
	if ((integer)(vFltRate = (llAngleBetween( llGetLocalRot(), vRotTarget ) / (vFltRate / 5.0)))){
		rotation vRotStep = llAxisAngle2Rot( llRot2Axis( vRotTarget / llGetLocalRot() ),
		                    (1.0 / vFltRate) * llRot2Angle( vRotTarget / llGetLocalRot() ) );
		vFltRate = (integer)vFltRate;
		do{
			llSetLocalRot( vRotStep * llGetLocalRot() );
		}while (--vFltRate);
	}
	llSetLocalRot( vRotTarget );
} //-- for fixed time on any rotation try llSetKeyframedMotion`} lang="lsl" /></div>
